16
00:01:51.280 --> 00:02:05.560
[George] Backslash and backslash and Taft possessed a scholarly, contemplative mind that flourished in the quiet study of constitutional jurisprudence, where decisions were guided by precedent and reasoned legal argument rather than emotional appeal.

17
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:17.560
[George] He preferred the deliberate, dignified atmosphere of appellate chambers to the raucous clamor of political conventions, backslash and backslash n throughout his early legal career in Ohio.

18
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:26.760
[George] Taft was recognized by peers as an exceptionally fair-minded jurist who resisted political pressures from both party machines and corporate syndicates.

19
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:36.680
[George] If William Howard Taft lacked political ambition, his brilliant, fiercely determined wife Helen, Nellie Heron Taft had enough ambition for both of them.

20
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:47.640
[George] Nellie was a cultured, independent Cincinnati woman who had visited the White House as a teenager and decided on the spot that she would marry a man who would become President of the United States.

21
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:55.800
[George] Whenever judicial appointments beckoned, Nellie steered her husband away from the bench and toward national executive administration.

22
00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:05.320
[George] In 1900, President William McKinley summoned Judge Taft to Washington and asked him to accept an impossible mission.

23
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:11.320
[George] Become the first civilian governor general of the Philippines following the bloody Philippine American War.

