[George] Taft proved himself an extraordinary colonial administrator, establishing civil liberties, building public infrastructure, and earning the genuine affection of the Filipino population.

30
00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.040
[George] He traveled thousands of miles across the islands on horseback.

31
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:17.440
[George] Listening to grievances and demonstrating that American administration was dedicated to public welfare, backslash and backslash and Taft's genuine affection for the Filipino people laid the groundwork for peaceful self-governance and earned him the lifelong loyalty of local leaders.

32
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.920
[George] In 1904, Roosevelt summoned Taft back to Washington to serve as Secretary of War.

33
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:40.400
[George] Taft quickly became TR's premier troubleshooter, a universal administrative problem solver whom Roosevelt dispatched to oversee the construction of the Panama Canal, govern rebellious Cuba under temporary occupation, and negotiate diplomatic accords with Japan.

34
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.040
[George] The two men were inseparable friends, complementing each other perfectly.

35
00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.240
[George] TR was the fiery, impulsive visionary.

36
